#47500
"Just Inside A Rotting Stump"
"The weathered wood of the marred tree twists down and about the entrance,
sheltering the small hollow of the trunk.  The smell of dirt and musky decay
hangs upon the moist air, and the muddy soil is blanketed by wet leaves,
stirring and whispering in the occasional gusts of wind from without.  The
ground dips down to the north, below the grasp of gnarled roots, a small
passageway lined with soft and fresh-dug earth.
"
