area of tall, lush ferns, their delicate green fronds bedewed with beaded
moisture.  Pines of all sizes crowd close together, hovering over the rise
protectively, while still more brambles fill the spaces between, forbidding
movement to the north and west.  A blur of movement, caught from the corner of
an eye, is there and gone before it is ever seen.
