#47503
"Wisps of Rising Smoke"
"Regal pines crowd close together, standing tall and straight and silent like
mute sentinels guarding their charge.  Beneath the canopy of intertwining
limbs, the undergrowth is less apparent, just a few scant bushes and a lone
vine that curls around what at first appears to be the remains of a felled
sapling.  Oddly enough, wispy fingers of smoke drift upward from the small
stump, only to dissipate into nothingness a few feet off the ground.  The
heavy scent of burning wood permeates the damp, cool air.
