#47513
"A Smoky Chamber"
"With walls of solid-packed earth, this chamber is clouded by a dull haze of
smoke, likely from the fireplace that dominates an alcove to the north.  The
ceiling slopes upward away from the walls, with dozens of roots dangling down
out of the enmeshed soil, all leading into a central circle...  a hollow log
through which the accumulated smoke slowly rises and disperses to the forest
without.  Scattered about the room are various broken chests and other
scavenger's treasures, the most striking of which is the wheel-less body of a
horse-drawn wagon.  The hollow narrows to the south where a barrier of
branches blocks further progress, while to the west the darkness of a tunnel
awaits beyond the dim fire's glow.
"
