#47515
"Circular Chamber"
"This large, circular chamber bears exits in all four directions, beneath the
hanging forest of vine-like roots.  The floor is strewn with cloth, some of it
the now-spoiled remnants of fine cotton, crumpled into a variety of beds and
cushions.  Large and imposing wooden arms from the trees above weave their way
in and out of the soil, appearing more frequently to the east.  Upon the base
of the southern wall, a crumbled hole marks the entrance to a slanting tunnel,
narrow and crossed with roots that one might, with effort, be able to crawl or
climb around.  To the north, several overlapping branches have been tied
together with a crudely fashioned rope, just large enough to encompass the
narrow tunnel portal.
"
